Z||000002||Cooter||10-25-2000||11:45 PM||||My dad has an 88 Reatta. Very nice car! Of everything we have fixed at the body shop, it is one of the best and heaviest built unibody cars we've seen. The car is heavy, but performance is still pretty good. The touch screen controls are neat- when they work! His quit working, but a friend fixed it with a new output transistor on the video. I have heard from a couple of people that GM didn't make enough of them to pay for the tooling equipment that it took to build them. Imagine that- GM abandons a great car because projected sales might have been low for one model year.||||reg||1
