Z||000013||Black88GT||10-26-2000||09:06 AM||||Reatta's are sloooooow.  They use the 3.8L V6.  I have tried to get one of them to race me about 3 different times, but they never will.  Usually old people drive them (go figure).<P>I have heard from mechanics they are very reliable.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||10-26-2000||09:44 AM||||My Mom has a red one that's fully loaded.  I thought it was small and comfortable untill I got my GT. That thing has a big trunk and lots of room behind the seat for a kick gass stereo.  She's had it maintained by having a neighbor take it to work.  He's a service manager at a Buick Dealership.  That makes every trip to the shop a succesfull one.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  She tried racing me once, but alls I heard was her tires peeling out and I got traction and pulled ahead.(technique)  She used to have a Ninja that blew away the Nighthawk I used to have though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-26-2000).]||||reg||1
