Z||000018||william_thorniii||10-26-2000||12:46 PM||||Tigger,<P>That is odd... Pontiac's orignal target market for the Fiero was females 18-35.  I always envisioned the Fiero as the predecessor of the Reatta, but the Reatta as being bigger and more of a mans car... funny.  <P>On a side note... Did you grow up looking at that immaculate 87 GT (w/o spoiler), med-red metallic that used to park at the Chevrolet Avenue Delco Plant?  Man I loved that car!  Never talked to the owner though.... :~(<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000019||Tigger||10-26-2000||01:36 PM||||WTIII,<P>Nope, I don't think I've seen that one...   <P>Everytime someone mentions the Reatta or I see one, I associate it with that girl back in HS, maybe that's why? I don't know.  But, I can see a middle to upper class guy driving a Reatta to the golf course.||||reg||1
